Status - Overview: render the System card as widgets when the Apex theme is active

luci-theme-apex shows the System card as four grouped widgets (Hardware,
Software, Time, Load Average) instead of the stock nine-row table. A theme cannot
supply that markup hack-free: the card is rendered client-side by this include
(owned by luci-mod-status; a second copy in the theme package would be an apk
file conflict) from live ubus data, so the markup has to come from here.

The theme in use is read on every render from L.env.media (set by the luci-base
header template), so switching themes needs no reboot and no reload logic:
  - Apex (/luci-static/apex): widgets (ax-sys-* classes, styled by the theme's
    cascade.css; semantic dl/dt/dd + h4 + role="meter"; all strings via _()).
  - any other theme: the stock table below, byte-identical to before (verified
    against the minified build; no extra request on that path).
Load bars are the load per CPU (1.00 = every core busy, clamped); the exact load
is always printed. The CPU count is read once per page load from
/sys/devices/system/cpu/online (ACL: patch 0003) and cached; if unreadable it
falls back to 1 CPU. "Firmware Version" stays the 0001 behaviour (release
description only); the LuCI revision is its own row. Local Time is shown as
YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS in the router's configured time zone (24 h unless the system
hour-cycle setting says otherwise; "UTC" is appended when no zone is configured);
the stock path keeps its own formatter.

Applies to: https://git.openwrt.org/project/luci.git
            @ 350fc919675bb62e415927afff65697fcb8f775d (pinned in feeds.conf.default)
Applied by: tools/cw-apply-feed-patches.sh (patch -p1, zero fuzz - the build
            fails if upstream changes these lines; re-port it then). Applies
            on top of 0001 (filename order).
Upstream status: not submitted (CleanWRT-specific).

